":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.12235678362154259,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":100.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.16818619998684126,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03205667395652255,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":46.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.050479997,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":33.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Novavax, Inc., a biotechnology company, engages in the discovery, development, and commercialization of vaccines to prevent serious infectious diseases in the United States, Europe, and internationally. The company commercializes Nuvaxovid, a COVID-19 vaccine; and R21 Matrix-M adjuvant malaria vaccine. It has license and collaboration agreements with Sanofi, Pfizer Inc., Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited, and Serum Life Sciences Limited for the to develop, manufacture, and commercialize the COVID-19 vaccine. The company was incorporated in 1987 and is headquartered in Gaithersburg, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John Charles Jacobs M.B.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 749 people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 36%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $48K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Novavax, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.8B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -17% over the past three years and +41% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -72% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $250M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +58.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 20\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.0% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 4.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +58.2% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-1.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 40% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Valued at a 175% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Novavax (NVAX) stock trades up, here is why","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nasdaq/nvax/news/why-up-down/novavax-nvax-stock-trades-up-here-is-why-2","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992857.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"B. Riley Financial Reaffirms \u201cBuy\u201d Rating for Novavax (NASDAQ:NVAX)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/b-riley-financial-reaffirms-buy-rating-for-novavax-nasdaqnvax.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793980878.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"NVAX Stock Falls 8% Despite Q3 Earnings & Sales Beat, Costs Decline","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/nvax-stock-falls-8-despite-135800896.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973480.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title"